Subject: [adegenet-forum] [adegenet forum] hw.test on genind object
In-Reply-To: <mailman.11.1438855214.2519.adegenet-forum@lists.r-forge.r-project.org>
References: <mailman.11.1438855214.2519.adegenet-forum@lists.r-forge.r-project.org>
Message-ID: <A119CF3F-2F23-4AF9-B8E0-2A80645F2A60@science.oregonstate.edu>

This is due to an issue in pegas where it expects the alleles to be in numerical order for micro satellites.

Until it's fixed, I have made a workaround here: https://gist.github.com/zkamvar/95af8adaf1b3f01a4995

Copy + paste the function into your R console and then use resort_microsat(myData) for the workaround.

Cheers,
Zhian

